# The repo-root .gitignore carries a bare `data/` rule for datasets. A pattern
# that ends in a slash and contains no other slash is NOT path-anchored, so it
# matched every directory named `data` anywhere in the tree — including the
# Kotlin package net/hermes/deck/data/. Three commits therefore shipped an app
# that no longer builds from a fresh clone, while it built fine here because
# the files were on disk. Re-include it from this fork-owned file; a deeper
# .gitignore wins over the root one, so upstream's file stays untouched.
!app/src/main/kotlin/net/hermes/deck/data/

*.apk
build/
.gradle/
*.keystore
.kotlin/
local.properties
# Staged debug APK for durable auth-download delivery (reports/by-task artifact, not a tracked binary)
